# Domain architecture

Keep these concerns **strictly decoupled**:

| Concern | Primary home (directory) |
|--------|----------------|
| Math (forward + reverse calculations, units, water, etc.) | `src/features/label/LabelMathResolver.ts`, `src/features/label/peptideMath.ts`, `src/features/label/domain/` |
| String building / layout structure | `src/features/label/LabelComposer.ts`, `LabelLayoutEngine.ts`, `templates/` |
| On-screen / print rendering | `src/features/label/LabelPreview.tsx` (and related CSS) |
| Orchestration of I/O (export, save, load) | Use cases in `src/app/`, depending only on port interfaces in `src/shared/ports.ts` |
| Wiring concrete adapters into a use case | The composition root `src/app/exportLabelPng.ts` — the one place in `src/app` allowed to import `src/platform` |
| Shared React state around a use case | `src/app/use*.ts` (e.g. `useLabelExport.ts`) — a genuine hook, shared by `label` and `customDesign`, so it cannot live in either feature |
| Browser APIs (storage, canvas, download, DOM query) | Adapters in `src/platform/`, implementing those ports |
| Derived / display values shown in a component | A pure view-model or presenter function the component calls, per the Humble Object rule in `testing-vitest.mdc` |

These boundaries are enforced by `no-restricted-imports` blocks in [eslint.config.js](../../eslint.config.js) — that config is the executable copy of this table. When a row changes, change the matching block in the same edit; do not let the two describe different boundaries.

The label math, composition, and template modules live in the feature root rather than a `domain/` directory, so the lint block enumerates `src/features/label/*.ts` and `src/features/label/templates/*.ts` (excluding `use*.ts` and tests) instead of relying on a path convention. React **type** imports are allowed there and in `src/print` / `src/shared`; React **values** are not.

Do not move calculation logic into the preview for convenience, or preview-specific hacks into the resolver. Do not call a browser API (`localStorage`, `IndexedDB`, `canvas`, `FileReader`, `document.*`) directly from a domain or app module — go through a port so the logic stays testable without a DOM.

## Defensive math (`LabelMathResolver`)

- Handle **forward** math (e.g. draw units) and **reverse** math (e.g. required water) explicitly and safely.
- **Never echo raw user input** into auto-calculated placeholders or derived fields in a way that masks the real computed value.
- **Fail gracefully** on invalid or incomplete inputs (clear UX, no silent wrong numbers).

## Global preferences

Settings such as **date format** (MM/DD/YYYY, YYYYMMDD, etc.) are **global preferences** carried in the label model / form state and passed through—avoid hard-coding formats inside isolated UI leaves.
